# Post-D25 (fault-catch removed): capture the fault as `Result[int, ArithError]`
# via the D26 fallible `*!` and match on the outcome. Axis: `+!/-!/*!` overflow
# via Route B (capture at destination). Non-literal operand so const-fold can't
# elide the fault. Runs on C + LLVM (bootstrap: fauld_catch_overflow_migrated).
void main():
    int big = 9223372036854775807
    Result[int, ArithError] r = big *! 2
    match r:
        case Ok(v):    print(f"{v}")
        case Error(_): print("-1")
    Result[int, ArithError] ok = 3 *! 4
    match ok:
        case Ok(v):    print(f"{v}")
        case Error(_): print("-1")
